# Networking Stack Conventions

## Address plan

- AWS cloud supernet: `10.0.0.0/11` (see workspace `docs/network-allocations.yaml`).
- Account / landscape block: `/20`.
- Regional VPC (`tf-vpc` `vpc_cidr`): `/21` (one half of the account `/20` per region).
- Subnets inside the `/21`: public `/25`, private `/24`, isolated `/25` (up to 3 AZs).

## VPC

Three-tier subnet design:

- **public** — Internet-facing (ALB, NAT Gateway).
- **private** — Application workloads (ECS services).
- **isolated** — Databases (RDS, DocDB) and internal-only services.

Standard VPC inputs (minimal = omit `availability_zone_ids` → 1 AZ):

```hcl
inputs = {
  vpc_cidr                = "10.0.0.0/21"  # regional /21 from the account /20
  create_internet_gateway = true
  create_nat_gateways     = true
  retention_in_days       = 7   # higher in prod (e.g. 30)
}
```

Pass `availability_zone_ids` with 2–3 AZ IDs when you need multi-AZ. VPC Flow Logs are part of `tf-vpc`; keep `retention_in_days` proportional to environment criticality.

Update `docs/network-allocations.yaml` when assigning a new `/20` or `/21`.

## ALB

```hcl
inputs = {
  detail                 = "<descriptor>"
  certificate_arn        = dependency.tls.outputs.certificate_arn
  vpc_id                 = dependency.vpc.outputs.vpc_id
  subnet_ids             = dependency.vpc.outputs.public_subnet_ids
  vpc_security_group_ids = [dependency.vpc.outputs.public_security_group_id]

  applications = [
    {
      app_alias         = "<app>"
      health_check_path = "/<app>/health"
      target_port       = 3001
      priority          = 2  # unique per ALB
    }
  ]
}
```

`priority` must be unique across applications on the same ALB. Health check paths follow `/{app_alias}/health` unless the app dictates otherwise.

## VPC Lattice associations

Most landscapes use `lattice_vpc_association/` to attach the local VPC to the Hub-shared service network. Do not modify `lattice_network` (lives in `agora`); subscriber accounts only consume the share.

## Cross-account / cross-landscape

Cross-account access (e.g. mnemosyne RDS over Lattice, Janus DNS) uses pre-provisioned IAM roles assumed in the target account. Do not introduce new cross-account roles without principal engineer review.

## Anti-patterns

- Public subnets for application workloads.
- ALB without HTTPS / certificate.
- Modifying `vpc_cidr` after launch (causes destroy/recreate of the entire VPC).
